course: dictionary
lesson: 12461
title: Deficiency: not having enough
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A deficiency is a lack of something you need. If you have a deficiency, you do not have enough of it. Look for clue words like «lack» or «not enough» near the word.
explain: «Her diet had a vitamin deficiency, so she felt tired and ill.» The words tired and ill are clues. Her body was missing something it needed, so a deficiency means not having enough of a needed thing.
explain: Deficiency can also mean a weakness or fault. «The report listed several deficiencies in the work.» Ask yourself what would fit here: faults or missing parts. Try swapping in «faults» to check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A deficiency is a lack of something that is needed.
fact: A deficiency can also be a weakness or fault in something.
fact: A vitamin deficiency means not getting enough of a vitamin, which can make you ill.
fact: Too little vitamin C can cause scurvy, a sickness that comes from a lack of this vitamin.
fact: In maths, a deficiency is a shortfall: how much less than is needed.
exercise: What does deficiency mean? | A kind of bright light | *A lack of something that is needed | A loud noise | A large amount of something
exercise: «The report listed several deficiencies in the work.» What does deficiencies mean here? | Long and difficult words | Extra pages of praise | *Faults or things that are missing | Happy ideas
exercise: In maths, what is a deficiency? | A kind of shape | The biggest number in a set | The number of times you add something | *The amount something falls short of what is needed
test: Which word means nearly the same as deficiency? | Feast | Surplus | *Shortage | Brightness
test: Which example shows a deficiency? | Ruby ate a big dinner and felt full | Priya finished the race first | Leo got a new bike for his birthday | *Sam has not had enough iron in his food and feels weak
exam: «The team's deficiencies were clear: they had too few players.» What does deficiencies mean here? | Excellent skills | Winning ways | *Things that are missing or lacking | Loud cheers from the crowd
